\pard\sb320\sa120\cf8\b\fs28 5.  How to Add a New Roll Number\par

\pard\sb60\sa60\cf0\b0\fs22 To add a new student (e.g., Roll 105), do the following:\par

\pard\sb60\par

\pard\sb240\sa80\cf2\b\fs24 Step A \f1\emdash  \f0 Insert into N_RollCall\par
\trowd\trgaph200\trrh1\trpaddl200\trpaddr200\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\clcfpat13\clcbpat25\clbrdrl\brdrw20\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrt\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2 \cellx9360 
\pard\intbl\sb20\sa20\cf12\b0\f2\fs20 INSERT INTO N_RollCall VALUES (105, 'Pooja', 88);\cf0\f0\fs22\par
\cf12\f2\fs20 COMMIT;\cf0\f3\fs22\cell\row 
\pard\sb80\f0\par

\pard\sb240\sa80\cf2\b\fs24 Step B \f1\emdash  \f0 Run the PL/SQL Block Again (Step 7)\par

\pard\sb60\sa60\cf0\b0\fs22 Run the same PL/SQL block from Step 7. It will automatically detect Roll 105 as new and insert it into O_RollCall.\par

\pard\sb80\par

