\pard\sb320\sa120\cf8\b\fs28 6.  How to Remove a Roll Number\par

\pard\sb60\sa60\cf0\b0\fs22 To remove a student record, you can delete from either or both tables.\par

\pard\sb60\par

\pard\sb240\sa80\cf2\b\fs24 Option A \f1\emdash  \f0 Delete from N_RollCall only\par

\pard\sb60\sa60\cf0\b0\fs22 Removes the student from the New table (O_RollCall is NOT affected):\par

\pard\sb60\par
\trowd\trgaph200\trrh1\trpaddl200\trpaddr200\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\clcfpat13\clcbpat25\clbrdrl\brdrw20\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrt\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2 \cellx9360 
\pard\intbl\sb20\sa20\cf12\f2\fs20 DELETE FROM N_RollCall WHERE Roll = 105;\cf0\f0\fs22\par
\cf12\f2\fs20 COMMIT;\cf0\f3\fs22\cell\row 
\pard\sb80\f0\par

\pard\sb240\sa80\cf2\b\fs24 Option B \f1\emdash  \f0 Delete from O_RollCall only\par

\pard\sb60\sa60\cf0\b0\fs22 Removes the student from the Old/merged table:\par

\pard\sb60\par
\trowd\trgaph200\trrh1\trpaddl200\trpaddr200\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\clcfpat13\clcbpat25\clbrdrl\brdrw20\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrt\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2 \cellx9360 
\pard\intbl\sb20\sa20\cf12\f2\fs20 DELETE FROM O_RollCall WHERE Roll = 105;\cf0\f0\fs22\par
\cf12\f2\fs20 COMMIT;\cf0\f3\fs22\cell\row 
\pard\sb80\f0\par

\pard\sb240\sa80\cf2\b\fs24 Option C \f1\emdash  \f0 Delete from BOTH tables\par

\pard\sb60\sa60\cf0\b0\fs22 Completely removes the student from both tables:\par

\pard\sb60\par
\trowd\trgaph200\trrh1\trpaddl200\trpaddr200\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3
\clcfpat13\clcbpat25\clbrdrl\brdrw20\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrt\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrr\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2\clbrdrb\brdrw8\brdrs\brdrcf2 \cellx9360 
\pard\intbl\sb20\sa20\cf12\f2\fs20 DELETE FROM N_RollCall WHERE Roll = 105;\cf0\f0\fs22\par
\cf12\f2\fs20 DELETE FROM O_RollCall WHERE Roll = 105;\cf0\f0\fs22\par
\cf12\f2\fs20 COMMIT;\cf0\f3\fs22\cell\row 
\pard\sb80\f0\par

